/-!
# The quotient map and inertia characterization of `G_{K,S}`

Let `K` be a number field and `S` a set of finite places of `K`. The file
`TauCeti.NumberTheory.NumberField.RestrictedRamification.Basic` defines the maximal extension
`K_S` of `K` unramified outside `S` (`maxUnramifiedOutside`) and its Galois group
`G_{K,S} = Gal(K_S / K)` (`galoisGroupS`). This file equips `G_{K,S}` with its quotient map from
`Gal(Ω / K)`, its functorial transition maps `G_{K,T} → G_{K,S}` for `S ⊆ T`, the local-to-global
decomposition maps `G_{K_v} → G_{K,S}`, and the characterization of `G_{K,S}` as the quotient of
the absolute Galois group `G_K` by the closed subgroup generated by all inertia subgroups at places
outside `S`.

The inclusion `inertiaOutsideSubgroup K S ≤ K_S.fixingSubgroup` follows from
`IntermediateField.absoluteGaloisGroupMap_mem_fixingSubgroup_of_notMem_ramifiedSupport`: every
element of `K_S` lies in a finite subextension unramified outside `S`, so local inertia at `v ∉ S`
fixes it along every embedding `Kˢ →ₐ[K] K_vˢ`. For the reverse inclusion, take any element `x`
fixed by `inertiaOutsideSubgroup K S` and let `L = K(x)`. For each `v ∉ S` and each prime `w` of
`𝓞 L` above `v`, choosing an embedding `L_w →ₐ[K_v] K_vˢ` and extending `L → L_w → K_vˢ` to
`τ : Kˢ →ₐ[K] K_vˢ` shows that local inertia at `v` fixes the image of `L`, hence the whole image
of `L_w` by the semi-local decomposition `K_v ⊗_K L ≃ ∏_{w ∣ v} L_w`. Thus `L_w / K_v` is
unramified, so `e(w | v) = 1` for every `w` over `v`, meaning `L` is unramified outside `S` and
`x ∈ K_S`.

## Main definitions

* `TauCeti.RestrictedRamification.restrictGaloisGroupS`: the continuous surjective restriction
  homomorphism `Gal(Ω / K) →ₜ* G_{K,S}`.
* `TauCeti.RestrictedRamification.galoisGroupSMap`: for `S ⊆ T`, the continuous surjective
  transition homomorphism `G_{K,T} →ₜ* G_{K,S}`.
* `TauCeti.RestrictedRamification.localToGaloisGroupS`: for a finite place `v` and an embedding
  `τ : Kˢ →ₐ[K] K_vˢ`, the continuous decomposition map `G_{K_v} →ₜ* G_{K,S}`.
* `TauCeti.RestrictedRamification.inertiaOutsideSubgroup`: the closed subgroup of `G_K` generated
  by the images of local inertia subgroups at all finite places `v ∉ S` along all embeddings
  `Kˢ →ₐ[K] K_vˢ`.

## Main results

* `TauCeti.RestrictedRamification.isQuotientMap_restrictGaloisGroupS`: the restriction map
  `Gal(Ω / K) → G_{K,S}` is a topological quotient map.
* `TauCeti.RestrictedRamification.localToGaloisGroupS_eq_one_of_mem_inertia`: for `v ∉ S`, the
  decomposition map `G_{K_v} → G_{K,S}` kills the local inertia subgroup.
* `TauCeti.RestrictedRamification.fixingSubgroup_maxUnramifiedOutside_eq_inertiaOutsideSubgroup`:
  the fixing subgroup of `K_S` in `G_K` equals `inertiaOutsideSubgroup K S`.
* `TauCeti.RestrictedRamification.ker_restrictGaloisGroupS_eq_inertiaOutsideSubgroup`: the kernel
  of `G_K → G_{K,S}` is `inertiaOutsideSubgroup K S`.
* `TauCeti.RestrictedRamification.existsUnique_comp_restrictGaloisGroupS_eq`: universal property
  of `G_{K,S}` for continuous homomorphisms from `G_K` to a `T₁` topological group killing local
  inertia outside `S`.

## References

* J. S. Milne, *Arithmetic Duality Theorems*, 2nd ed., Chapter I, §4.
* J. Neukirch, *Algebraic Number Theory*, Chapter II, §9.
-/

public section

noncomputable section

open IntermediateField IsDedekindDomain NumberField TauCeti
